    "heading": "Good to know",
    "text": "Each suggestion uses the actual activity for the last 12 months when there was any. If there was none, it uses last year's budget. Then it adds the inflation adjustment and rounds to whole dollars.\nIf your books cover less than a year, the actuals are scaled up to a full year, and the reason says how many months they covered.\nA reserve contribution is never suggested below last year's budget. The line is marked Reserve floor.\nEvery number on the page is calculated by the app. The AI summary only describes those numbers. If it uses a figure that isn't on the page, the summary is thrown away and only the list of changes is shown.\nLines left at $0 aren't saved.\nOpening next fiscal year follows your books: a yearly period if your periods are yearly, monthly periods if they're monthly, starting in the same month your fiscal year does. On Fiscal periods the new year shows \"Starts\" with its first day and can't be closed until it has started.",
